<section id="demo" class="wrap" aria-labelledby="demo-title" data-section="demo">
  <div class="graticule meta"><span>signature demo</span><span>replayed EMG · LDA in the browser</span></div>
  <h2 id="demo-title">Hold to contract</h2>
  <div class="col">
    <p>
      A myoelectric classifier trained on day 1 meets the same person's muscles on day 29, after the electrodes have been
      taken off and put back on. It gets worse, for real. Then you recalibrate it with three holds, and it recovers.
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Pick a gesture.</strong> <span class="meta">Hand Close · Hand Open · Thumb–Index Opposition · Index Finger Extension</span></li>
      <li><strong>Hold to contract.</strong> The real recorded EMG for that gesture replays; the classifier labels each 200 ms window live.</li>
      <li><strong>Skip to day 29.</strong> Same participant, same day-1 model. Watch the accuracy drop.</li>
      <li><strong>Recalibrate.</strong> Hold three times; the class means and covariance update in your browser.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="todo">TODO(phase 4): the interactive version and the population results across all 43 participants.</p>
    <p class="meta honesty">
      Replayed public data: GRABMyo, day 1 vs day 29. Classifier: LDA on time-domain features, running in your browser.
      Not MyoCopilot's production model.
    </p>
    <p class="meta cite">
      Data: Jiang, N., Pradhan, A., &amp; He, J. (2024). Gesture Recognition and Biometrics ElectroMyogram (GRABMyo)
      (version 1.1.0). PhysioNet. <a href="https://doi.org/10.13026/89dm-f662">doi:10.13026/89dm-f662</a>. CC BY 4.0.
      Pradhan, A., He, J. &amp; Jiang, N. Multi-day dataset of forearm and wrist electromyogram for hand gesture recognition
      and biometrics. Sci Data 9, 733 (2022). <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01836-y">doi:10.1038/s41597-022-01836-y</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">
      This is the idea behind <a href="/work/myocopilot">MyoCopilot</a> and
      <a href="/work/edge-decoder-drift">edge-decoder-drift</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

